---
import { BACKDOOR_MAP_PUBLICATION } from '../../data/backdoor-map';
import BackDoorMapLayout from '../../layouts/BackDoorMapLayout.astro';

const description = 'How to make a data access, correction, or deletion request for BackDoor Map.';
---

<BackDoorMapLayout
    title="BackDoor Map Data Requests | Cold Forge Works LLC"
    description={description}
    heading="Data Requests"
    canonicalUrl={BACKDOOR_MAP_PUBLICATION.urls.dataRequests}
    showDocumentStatus
    documentUpdatedDate="October 12, 2026"
>
    <section aria-labelledby="delete-backup-account">
        <h2 id="delete-backup-account">Delete your backup account and cloud backups</h2>
        <p>
            <a href="/backdoor-map/delete-account">Request account deletion</a> without reinstalling the app.
            Confirm ownership with a fresh code sent to your backup-account email, then confirm permanent deletion.
            Never send that code to support. You can also use App information &gt; Account backup &gt; Delete backup
            account in the app.
        </p>
        <p>
            This removes your email account and its current and previous active cloud backups. Saved places on your
            phones, exported files and separately submitted community contributions are not deleted. Provider
            recovery copies and required security records may remain separately. Pausing backup or signing out is
            not account deletion.
        </p>
        <p>
            Our encrypted server recovery copies can still contain older account data. We keep one verified copy
            for each of the latest seven days with a successful backup; failed or missed backups can extend that
            period. Rotated Google Drive copies normally remain in Trash for another 30 days. These copies are
            restricted and separate from active account backups. See the <a href="/backdoor-map/privacy#retention-deletion">Privacy Policy's retention details</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
            If you cannot access your email or confirmation is unavailable, contact support below. An unverified
            message cannot authorize deletion of someone else's account. If a deletion response is lost, contact
            support before creating another account; do not assume deletion succeeded or was canceled.
        </p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="request-process">
        <h2 id="request-process">Request access, correction, or deletion</h2>
        <p>
            Email <a href={`mailto:${BACKDOOR_MAP_PUBLICATION.supportEmail}`}>
                {BACKDOOR_MAP_PUBLICATION.supportEmail}
            </a> to request access to, correction of, or deletion of BackDoor Map information where applicable. Include
            the type of request and enough detail for us to understand what records may be involved.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="anonymous-records">
        <h2 id="anonymous-records">Community records use a separate identity</h2>
        <p>
            Community contributions are associated with a pseudonymous installation identifier rather than your
            optional backup account or a public profile. Signing in to backup does not prove ownership of community
            contributions. The app does not prominently display raw internal identifiers, and you do not
            need to locate one before contacting us.
        </p>
        <p>Details that may help us locate a relevant submission include:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>the building address;</li>
            <li>whether the request concerns a pin, vote, correction, reviewer note, or report;</li>
            <li>the approximate date and time of the activity;</li>
            <li>the app platform, version, and build; and</li>
            <li>a description of the submitted location or issue.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            We may ask for additional information to avoid changing or disclosing someone else's contribution. Some
            installation-linked records may not be identifiable without sufficient details, and we cannot promise to locate data
            that cannot reliably be connected to the information provided.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="local-data">
        <h2 id="local-data">Local places and exported files</h2>
        <p>
            Manage local Favorites, Recents, notes and personal pins in the app. Keep a successful backup or usable
            encrypted export before changing phones or reinstalling. Deleting local data does not remove an older
            cloud snapshot; manage cloud backups separately in Account backup. We cannot remotely erase exported
            files or recover a lost export key.
        </p>
        <p>Do not send support sign-in codes, recovery keys, passwords or private backup files.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="request-limits">
        <h2 id="request-limits">Limits and retention</h2>
        <p>
            A request may be limited where records must be retained for fraud prevention, legal compliance, security,
            vote integrity, or moderation history. Aggregate or anonymized information may remain after a request is
            completed. We will evaluate requests under applicable law and the circumstances of the record.
        </p>
        <p>For more detail, read the <a href="/backdoor-map/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    </section>
</BackDoorMapLayout>
